From b69c5cab81ed53c5fddf4a2ab588481f0e145f02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nfs2015-wine-cx-port <BmOdtQAYHaz36O85F8A@gcqd.fr>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 23:36:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] wine: Rosetta debug-register state + TF-based
 execution-breakpoint delivery

Port of c5ab37b from the wine-nfs2015-fix tree (a Wine 11.18 subset) onto this
CrossOver Wine 11.0 tree. Behaviour is intended to be identical; the differences
below are all consequences of 11.0 predating the 11.1x signal-handler rework.

 - server/mach.c: keep a per-thread debug-register shadow for translated
   processes so CONTEXT_DEBUG_REGISTERS reads agree with writes instead of
   returning zeros (previously a self write of dr7=0x155 read back as 0).
 - server/thread.{c,h}: system_flags becomes get_system_flags( thread ), which
   returns 0 for a translated AMD64 process in this mode so the suspended client
   owns its own DEBUG context, plus the rosetta_debug_regs[6] storage.
 - dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c: virtual_read_executable_byte(), a bounded
   instruction fetch that checks permissions and reads under virtual_mutex.
 - dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c: when DR7 enables an execution breakpoint,
   emulate delivery with the x86 trap flag and raise an in-process
   EXCEPTION_SINGLE_STEP carrying the matching DR6 bit. That is the only path
   this title can observe: PEB->BeingDebugged is false, so send_debug_event()
   returns immediately and no debug object is involved.

Gated by WINE_TF_EMULATION=1; AMD64 non-WoW, translated processes only.

Differences forced by the 11.0 tree:

 - 11.0 has no struct thread_data and no amd64_thread_data( data ); the
   accessor is amd64_thread_data(void) over ntdll_get_thread_data(). Every tf
   helper therefore drops its thread argument and operates on the current
   thread, which is what all of them did anyway. tf_thread_data() consequently
   cannot repeat 11.18's !thread->teb guard for TEB-less unix threads; it is no
   weaker than the surrounding 11.0 code, which already dereferences
   amd64_thread_data() unconditionally on these same paths.
 - 11.0 caches sysctl.proc_translated as is_rosetta2 (CW Hack 24256) earlier in
   signal_init_process(), before any handler is installed, so the mode flag is
   derived from that instead of adding a second sysctlbyname() call, and
   <sys/sysctl.h> is already included.
 - In 11.0 the "(possible) hardware breakpoint, fetch the debug registers"
   server round-trip and the single-step EFlags clear live in
   setup_raise_exception(), not in trap_handler() as in 11.18. The whole block
   is skipped while emulating, and trap_handler() clears EFlags bit 8 itself on
   the emulated path, which reproduces 11.18 exactly: the trap_handler path
   clears it and skips the fetch, and the restore_context path (which in 11.18
   reaches a setup_raise_exception that has no such block) does neither.
 - 11.0's leave_handler() has no __APPLE__ branch and its init_handler() never
   moves the macOS TSD base, so the 11.18 leave_handler() correction on
   trap_handler()'s handle_syscall_trap() early return has nothing to restore
   here and is deliberately not carried over; adding the call would instead
   reset %ds/%es, which is not part of this change.
 - CW HACK 22131, which fakes STATUS_SUCCESS when the server refuses a
   debug-register write under Rosetta, is left exactly as it is rather than
   duplicated or removed. In this mode it is simply unreachable: a self write
   no longer clears `self`, so no server call is made, and a cross-thread write
   now succeeds in server/mach.c, so ret is never STATUS_UNSUCCESSFUL. With
   WINE_TF_EMULATION unset it keeps working as before. The same hack in
   set_thread_wow64_context() is untouched because the mode is off under WoW.
---
